**Claim 1.**

A backlight structure for a display panel, comprising:

a housing having a bottom wall and sidewalls extending from a periphery of the bottom wall to define an accommodating cavity, the bottom wall defining a plane having a first corner, a second corner, a third corner, and a fourth corner;

a reflecting sheet disposed on the bottom wall within the accommodating cavity and having a light-reflecting surface facing away from the bottom wall, the light-reflecting surface having a first corner region corresponding to the first corner of the bottom wall and a central region spaced from the first corner region;

at least one light source arranged relative to the housing and configured to emit light toward the accommodating cavity;

a plurality of reflecting dots distributed across the light-reflecting surface of the reflecting sheet, each of the plurality of reflecting dots having a respective dot size and being configured to scatter at least a portion of the light incident thereon; and

an optical assembly disposed over the accommodating cavity and configured to receive light reflected and scattered from the light-reflecting surface;

wherein the plurality of reflecting dots are arranged such that the respective dot size of the reflecting dots progressively increases along a direction extending from the first corner region toward the central region, such that the reflecting dots located in the first corner region have a smaller dot size than the reflecting dots located in the central region, thereby compensating for a non-uniform luminance distribution across the display panel and improving overall luminance uniformity of light emitted from the optical assembly.
